From: Eureka bot <engg.eurekawireless@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jan 2026 14:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Fix MME crash when source eNB S1 context removed during
 handover
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MME crashed with assertion failure during S1/X2 handover:

  01/26 08:23:59.580: [mme] FATAL: mme_s11_handle_create_indirect_data_forwarding_tunnel_response:
  Assertion `source_ue' failed. (../src/mme/mme-s11-handler.c:1906)

## Root Cause

Race condition between GTP-C and S1AP processing:
1. MME sends Create Indirect Data Forwarding Tunnel Request to SGW
2. Source eNB sends UE CONTEXT RELEASE or HO CANCEL (S1 context removed)
3. SGW responds with Create Indirect Data Forwarding Tunnel Response
4. MME tries to find source_ue → NULL → CRASH

## Fix

Replace ogs_assert(source_ue) with graceful error handling:
- Log error with IMSI for debugging
- Call mme_ue_clear_indirect_tunnel() to cleanup indirect tunnel state
- Return gracefully instead of crashing

This matches the existing error handling pattern in the same file
(lines 1826-1830, 1844-1848, 1858-1862).

